{
  "title": "Calorie estimates: weigh inch-sized piece variants (knobs, chunks, ranges, fractions)",
  "description": "The parser now takes an inch-sized piece as the unit (\"1 3-inch piece of ginger\" -> unit \"3-inch piece\", \"1 3-4 inch chunk of ginger\" -> unit \"3-4 inch chunk\", \"Four 3-inch knobs fresh ginger\" -> unit \"3-inch knobs\"). bespoke.json weighs ginger's \"1/2 inch piece\", \"1 inch piece\", \"2 inch piece\" and \"3 inch piece\", but catalog::piece_unit only singularizes the first word and grams_per_piece matches exact keys, so \"3 inch knobs\", \"3 inch chunk\", \"3-4 inch chunk\" and \"3/4 inch piece\" fail with Unsupported quantity unit. \
These lines used to count as a bare piece. \
Compute inch pieces from the per-inch weight instead (size times the 1-inch weight, a range giving a calorie range, and chunk/knob/hunk treated as piece), rather than adding a key for each size. \
These variants are likely part of the +12 Unsupported quantity unit lines the parser change added to data/ingredient-catalog-audit.md; others may be sized loose measures (\"small handful\", \"large pinch\") for foods with no handful or pinch portion.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 4,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "nutrition",
    "catalog",
  ],
